## 2. Required Technical Skills & Competency Levels

### 2.1 Competency Framework (from Internal Craft Excellence Profiles)

The organization uses a P30–P90 leveling system with three distinct ML craft tracks:
1. **Machine Learning Engineer (MLE)** — focused on designing, developing, and implementing ML algorithms and models
2. **Machine Learning Systems Engineer (MLSE)** — specialized in engineering robust, scalable ML systems (70% engineering, 30% ML)
3. **Software Engineer (SWE)** — general software engineering with some ML exposure

**For the AI MLE Employee, targeting P50-equivalent autonomous capability:**

#### Programming & Software Engineering
| Skill | Level Required | Notes |
|-------|---------------|-------|
| Python | Expert | Primary language; production-quality code |
| Java/Kotlin | Proficient | For service integration, Spring/REST |
| SQL | Expert | Data manipulation, pipeline queries |
| PySpark | Proficient | Large-scale data processing (50+ TB) |
| Golang/TypeScript | Working knowledge | Platform integrations |

#### ML Frameworks & Libraries
| Framework | Level Required | Use Case |
|-----------|---------------|----------|
| PyTorch | Expert | Primary DL framework; distributed training (DDP, torchrun) |
| TensorFlow | Proficient | Model serving, TFX pipelines |
| HuggingFace Transformers | Expert | LLM fine-tuning, model loading |
| scikit-learn | Proficient | Classical ML, preprocessing |
| NumPy/Pandas | Expert | Data manipulation |
|ONNX | Working knowledge | Model portability and inference optimization |

#### Deep Learning & NLP/LLM Expertise
- Neural network architectures (BERT, SpanBERT, USE, encoder-decoder)
- LLM fine-tuning (PEFT, LoRA, full fine-tuning)
- Prompt engineering and RAG systems
- NLP/NLU (text classification, entity extraction, semantic search)
- Ranking models (learning-to-rank, DCN_V2, two-head architectures)
- Anomaly detection and time series analysis
- Recommendation systems (collaborative filtering, content-based)

#### Statistical Foundations
- Experimental design and A/B testing
- Bias-variance tradeoff analysis
- Statistical hypothesis testing
- Bayesian methods and probabilistic modeling
- Evaluation metrics (MRR, NDCG, precision/recall, F1)

#### MLOps & Infrastructure
- Distributed training orchestration (multi-node GPU clusters)
- Model serving architecture (online/batch inference)
- Feature store design and management
- CI/CD for ML pipelines
- Container orchestration (Kubernetes, Docker)
- Cloud infrastructure (AWS primarily: SageMaker, Lambda, SQS)

### 2.2 AI MLE Competency Adaptations

For an AI employee, additional competency requirements:

| Competency | Rationale |
|------------|-----------|
| **Specification parsing** | Must interpret YAML/JSON task specs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails from human-authored documents |
| **Autonomous experiment loop design** | Must be able to design mutation → scoring → keep/discard loops without human intervention |
| **Self-evaluation** | Must assess own confidence level and trigger escalation when below threshold |
| **Context grounding** | Must rapidly ingest codebase context, architectural patterns, and historical incident data |
| **Audit trail generation** | Must produce complete reasoning traces, experiment logs, and decision documentation |

