## 7. Gaps & Open Questions

1. **Model Card Standard:** No single organization-wide model card template was found — teams use ad-hoc documentation. The AI MLE should enforce a standardized model card as part of every deployment.

2. **Codebase access limitations:** Code search was unauthorized during this research. The AI MLE role definition should include specific repository access patterns (ML Studio modules repo, ML Platform infra repos, product-specific ML repos).

3. **Multi-cloud readiness:** The organization is expanding from AWS to GCP (ML Fabric on Kubernetes). The AI MLE must be cloud-agnostic in its tooling proficiency.

4. **LLM-native evaluation:** The evaluation landscape is actively evolving (AIX-eval EVaC, Rovo-eval, LLM-as-a-judge). The AI MLE should be built to adapt to new evaluation paradigms rapidly.

5. **Feature Store migration:** The organization is actively migrating from Tecton to MLFS. The AI MLE must understand both systems during the transition period.

