## 2. Guardrails and Escalation Policies

### 2.1 Model Performance Thresholds

Based on [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356) and [OPEX Monitoring and Alerting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ANALYTICS/pages/3346826368):

| **Metric Category** | **Threshold / Trigger** | **Action** |
|---------------------|------------------------|-----------|
| **Online Latency** | P50 > target + 20% | 🟡 Alert → AI MLE investigates, proposes mitigation |
| **Online Latency** | P99 > SLO breach |🔴 Page human → immediate incident response |
| **Offline Accuracy Drop** | > 5% degradation from baseline | 🟡 Trigger investigation + retraining evaluation |
| **Prediction Distribution Shift** | PSI > 0.25 (significant) | 🔴 Escalate — model serving may need pause |
| **Feature Drift** | KS test p< 0.05 or PSI 0.1–0.25 | 🟡 Alert + automated diagnosis |
| **Pipeline Failure Rate** | > 1% of runs fail | 🟢 Auto-restart;🟡 escalate if persistent |
| **Model Uptime** | < 99.5% | 🔴 Escalate to SRE + platform team |
| **Cost Anomaly** | > 30% above budget forecast | 🟡 Alert finance + engineering lead |

### 2.2 Data Quality Gates

Per [ML Observability Migration to ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6393498740):

- **Volume monitoring**: Track data volume changes; alert on > 20% deviation from baseline
- **Null/Coverage**: Alert when % non-null drops below historical baseline by > 30%
- **Schema validation**: Block pipeline on schema mismatch
- **Distribution shape**: Monitor mean, P1/P50/P99; alert on statistical drift
- **Binary features**: Alert when proportion of 1s vs 0s shifts significantly
- **Score health**: Alert if L1/L2 score distributions collapse to0 or show extreme spikes

### 2.3 Bias/Fairness Checkpoints

- **Pre-training gate**: Dataset balance assessment across protected attributes
- **Post-training gate**: Evaluate model fairness metrics (equalized odds, demographic parity) per slice
- **Pre-deployment gate**: Fairness audit sign-off required (🔴 human always)
- **Production monitoring**: Continuous fairness metric tracking with automated alerting

### 2.4 Compute Cost Guardrails

| **Resource** | **Budget Limit** | **Enforcement** |
|-------------|-----------------|-----------------|
| GPU training hours (per experiment) | Configurable cap per team | 🟢 Auto-terminate at limit |
| Total monthly compute | Budget ceiling with 80% warning | 🟡 Alert at 80%, block at 100% |
| Auto-scaling inference | Max replica count per model | 🟢 Hard cap enforced |
| Idle resource detection | > 2hr GPU idle | 🟢 Auto-release |

### 2.5 Escalation Paths

Per the [AI SDLC Governance Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AISDLC/pages/6849219616) and [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831):

```
Level 0 (Autonomous): Known patterns, within policy → AI MLE handles independently↓ (threshold breach or novel situation)
Level 1 (Confirm): Requires human MLE/TL review → Slack notification + approval flow
    ↓ (service degradation or SLO breach)
Level 2 (Escalate): Page on-call SRE → incident response protocol
    ↓ (cross-org impact or data breach)
Level 3 (Executive): Engineering leadership + legal/compliance
```

**AI-Specific Escalation Rules:**
- AI MLE **must escalate** when encountering decisions it hasn't seen before (novel patterns)
- AI MLE **must escalate** on any action that could affect customer data or PII
- AI MLE **cannot** make launch/rollback decisions unilaterally
- AI MLE **cannot** approve its own model for production — requires separate human reviewer
- Stalled or crashed AI MLE agents are auto-restarted by Symphony orchestration; ownership preserved

