## 7. Operational Monitoring of the AI MLE Itself

### 7.1 Agent Health Monitoring

Per [Agent Reliability Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AA7/pages/6097247892):

| **Health Signal** | **Monitoring** | **Action** |
|-----------------|---------------|-----------|
| Agent liveness | Heartbeat check | Auto-restart on failure |
| Decision quality drift | Periodic eval against golden datasets | Alert human supervisor |
| Action pattern anomaly | Behavioral baseline comparison | Flag for review |
| Budget consumption | Real-time spend tracking | Throttle or pause at limits |
| Escalation rate | Track % of tasks requiring human | Investigate if trending up (skill gap) or down (scope creep) |
| Task completion rate | Success/failure ratio over time | Investigate degradation |
| Reasoning coherence | Semantic drift detection on outputs | Alert on significant drift |

### 7.2 Continuous Improvement Loop

Per [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831) — The Symphony loop: **Watch → Bootstrap → Execute → Supervise → Close → Learn**

Each completed work item enriches the context layer, making the next execution smarter. The AI MLE improves with every task — no retraining required:
- Feedback loops (thumbs up/down, corrections from human reviewers)
- Observed outcomes (successful vs. failed experiments, deployments)
- Knowledge accumulation (domain expertise from resolved incidents)
- Governance gates for capability expansion (approvals for new skill grants)

