## 8. Summary: Key Differentiators from Human MLE

| **Dimension** | **Human MLE** | **AI MLE Employee** |
|--------------|--------------|---------------------|
| **Work pattern** | 8-hour day, context switches, meetings | Continuous 24/7 monitoring and execution |
| **Experiment velocity** | Limited by cognitive load | Parallel experiments, limited only by compute |
| **Decision authority** | Full authority within role scope | Three-tier (🟢/🟡/🔴) with explicit boundaries |
| **Accountability** | Self-directed with peer review | Auditable reasoning traces + human oversight |
| **Scaling** | Hire more humans | Spawn subordinate agents within policy |
| **Knowledge transfer** | Documentation, mentoring | Instant context sharing via ORBIT |
| **Failure mode** | Burnout, knowledge silos | Logic drift, policy boundary confusion |
| **Improvement** | Training, experience | Feedback loops, observed outcomes, no retraining |
| **Strategic thinking** | Core strength | Deferred to human MLE (IC6/IC7 layer) |
| **Novel research** | Creative exploration | 🔴 Human domain — AI MLE executes, doesn't design |

