## Executive Summary

This research establishes the comprehensive operational framework for a **Digital MLE (Machine Learning Engineer) AI Employee** — defining how the role operates within OpenStartup's organizational structure. Drawing from industry MLOps frameworks, internal Atlassian documentation on AI employee strategy, and established ML platform engineering practices, this document covers standard operating procedures, guardrails, escalation policies, success metrics, collaboration patterns, team structure, and failure mode mitigation.

**Key AI-Specific Finding:** Unlike a human MLE, the AI MLE operates under a **three-tier autonomy model** (🟢 Autonomous / 🟡 Confirm / 🔴 Human-required) as defined in the AI Employee Strategy. The AI MLE doesn't "wait for instructions" — it proactively manages its domain, escalates blockers, and surfaces insights, with human oversight through delegation and approval flows rather than direct prompting.

---

## 1. Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)

### 1.1 Model Development Lifecycle Gates

The AI MLE follows a structured MLOps lifecycle organized into three loops (per the [MLOps User Journey](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120208a96defdad944d9aa72853f83f516b6a/pages/4727324664)):

| **Phase** | **Gate Criteria** | **AI MLE Autonomy Level** |
|-----------|------------------|--------------------------|
| **Inner Loop: Experimentation** | Data exploration, feature engineering, model development, training with small datasets | 🟢 Autonomous — rapid iteration, logging all experiments |
| **Middle Loop: Validation** | Model evaluation against fairness/calibration/business metrics, reproducibility check, experiment registry | 🟡 Confirm — human reviews offline eval results before promotion |
| **Outer Loop: Production** | CI/CD pipeline pass, quality gates met, canary deployment successful, post-deployment verification (PDV) | 🔴 Human required for launch/rollback decisions |

**SOP: Model Promotion Criteria** (per [CI/CD for MLOps](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6726837663)):
1. Model passes all automated quality gates (accuracy thresholds, latency budgets, bias checks)
2. Model registered in MLflow with full metadata (training data version, hyperparameters, feature set)
3. A/B experiment results reviewed (statistical significance confirmed)
4. Canary deployment completes with quality score≥ threshold
5. Post-Deployment Verification (PDV) passes before full traffic ramp

**AI-Specific SOP Adaptations:**
- The AI MLE autonomously iterates the full fine-tuning pipeline (training data, recipe selection —LoRA vs. DoRA vs. SFT, loss function) for up to **12 hours before mandatory human review** ([AI Lab Review5/14](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LAB/pages/7036087684))
- All experiment decisions are logged with reasoning traces for human audit
- The AI MLE drafts the User Impact section of launch review docs autonomously but requires human sign-off on the actual launch decision

### 1.2 Code Review Standards for ML Code

| **Artifact** | **Review Protocol** | **AI MLE Role** |
|-------------|--------------------|--------------------|
| Training scripts | Automated linting + human peer review | 🟢 Generates,🟡 Submits for review |
| Feature engineering code | Data governance approval required | 🟡 Proposes, human validates compliance |
| Model serving code | Standard SWE code review + SRE sign-off | 🟡 Generates PR, human approves |
| Configuration changes | Automated validation against schema | 🟢 Autonomous for known patterns |
| Experiment notebooks | Reproducibility check (documented data + seeds) | 🟢 Autonomous with logging |

### 1.3 Experiment Approval Process

Per the [Digital MLE Vision](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/7051610727):

1. **Experiment Design** — 🟢 Autonomous: AI MLE designs A/B experiments and offline evals
2. **Resource Allocation** — 🟡 Confirm: Compute budget approval for large training runs
3. **Flight Monitoring** — 🟢 Autonomous: Monitors Statsig scorecards, summarizes metric movements
4. **Interpretation** — 🟡 Confirm: Human validates regression interpretation and launch doc
5. **Launch/Rollback Decision** — 🔴 Human: Always requires human authorization

### 1.4 Production Deployment Procedures

Per [Model Lifecycle MLOps Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020cd3f787132154dc3b533d4df685f7759/pages/5132476911) and [Model Deployments in ML Lifecycle](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6122166900):

1. **Pre-deployment**: Performance profiling job passes in staging/launchpad
2. **Canary rollout**: Feature gate enables for regression-user group first
3. **Canary evaluation**: Judge scoring + action sequence validation + drift comparison + reliability deltas
4. **Progressive rollout**: If canary score≥ threshold → widen; else → stop/rollback
5. **Post-deployment verification**: Evaluation dataset run against deployed model version
6. **Ramp-up**: AI MLE monitors serving latency against KR targets, generates ramp plan doc — human confirms ramp progression

