## 4. Cross-Functional Collaboration Patterns

### 4.1 Collaboration Map

Based on organizational patterns from [Senior MLE role descriptions](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SER/pages/6172987623), [Core ML Team Structure](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5459994030), and [K8s SRE One Pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~jgeeves/pages/6217103216):

| **Partner** | **Interaction Pattern** | **Frequency** | **AI MLE Autonomy** |
|------------|------------------------|---------------|---------------------|
| **Data Engineers** | Data pipeline health monitoring; feature quality validation; schema change coordination; data contract management | Continuous (automated) + weekly sync | 🟢 Monitoring; 🟡 Schema changes |
| **Platform/Infra (ML Platform)** | Serving infrastructure provisioning; GPU allocation; MLflow/ML Lens integration; deployment pipeline maintenance | On-demand + quarterly planning | 🟡 Resource requests; 🟢 Monitoring |
| **SRE Agent (Peer AI Employee)** | Incident co-response for ML services; shared on-call for ML infrastructure; deployment verification; latency optimization | Event-driven + daily health checks | 🟢 Peer coordination within policy |
| **Product Managers** | Feature prioritization input; experiment design review; business metric alignment; launch decisions | Sprint planning + experiment reviews | 🟡Proposals; 🔴 Launch decisions |
| **Research Scientists** | Novel approach evaluation; architecture exploration; state-of-the-art literature incorporation | Bi-weekly research reviews | 🟡 Evaluation; 🔴 Architecture choices |
| **Human MLE (Supervisor)** | Strategic direction; architecture decisions; approval flows; escalation handling | Continuous oversight loop | Reports to human MLE for🟡/🔴 decisions |

### 4.2 Communication Norms

Per the AI Employee Strategy's **Symphony orchestration layer**:

- **Proactive updates**: AI MLE posts daily summary to team channel (experiments run, results, blockers)
- **Escalation channel**: Dedicated Slack channel for 🟡/🔴 approval requests with structured context
- **Reasoning traces**: Every decision logged with full reasoning for human audit
- **Handoff protocol**: When AI MLE hits autonomy boundary, it provides full context pack to human reviewer
- **Peer collaboration rooms**: Structured interaction spaces for AI MLE ↔ SRE Agent coordination

### 4.3 Interaction with SRE Agent (Peer AI Employee)

Per [AI Lab Daily Sync](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LAB/pages/6173797971) and [AI Employee Strategy](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202027e1af5d30e94112880666ee62f9277a/pages/6742955831):

| **Scenario** | **SRE Agent Role** | **MLE Agent Role** | **Coordination** |
|-------------|-------------------|-------------------|-----------------|
| Model serving incident | Primary responder (infra) | Provides model context, suggests rollback version | Peer collaboration room |
| Latency optimization | Identifies infrastructure opportunities | Validates model-level optimizations | Joint PR submission |
| Deployment verification | Runs PDV infrastructure checks | Runs model quality checks | Sequential gate |
| Capacity planning | Forecasts infrastructure needs | Forecasts model scaling needs | Shared planning doc |

