## 5. Common Failure Modes and Mitigation Strategies

### 5.1 Training Instability

**Symptoms**: Loss divergence, NaN gradients, OOM errors, worker nodes reclaimed mid-run ([Unified Template Recommendation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/6537821624))

| **Failure Mode** | **Detection** | **Mitigation** | **AI MLE Action** |
|-----------------|--------------|----------------|-------------------|
| Loss divergence | Automated loss monitoring during training | Reduce learning rate; gradient clipping; checkpoint rollback | 🟢 Auto-adjust hyperparameters within bounds |
| NaN gradients | NaN check in training loop | Restart from last checkpoint; adjust initialization | 🟢 Auto-restart with adjusted config |
| OOM errors | CUDA memory monitoring | Reduce batch size; enable gradient accumulation; switch to smaller model | 🟢 Auto-scale down; 🟡 if persistent |
| Node reclamation | Cluster health monitoring | Checkpoint frequently; use spot-instance-aware training | 🟢 Auto-resume from checkpoint |
| Distributed training desync | Worker heartbeat monitoring | Restart failed workers; elastic training | 🟢 Auto-restart workers |

### 5.2 Data Distribution Shift

**Symptoms**: Model accuracy degradation, prediction distribution changes, feature value range shifts

Per [Data Drift Detection Architecture Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6866709029), [Model Drift Identification](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CA3/pages/1953707277), and internal drift detection frameworks:

| **Drift Type** | **Detection Method** | **Threshold** | **Mitigation** |
|---------------|---------------------|--------------|----------------|
| **Concept drift** (target relationship changes) | Online performance metric monitoring + error rate tracking | Accuracy drop > 5% sustained over 48hr | 🟡 Trigger retraining evaluation; human decides scope |
| **Data drift** (input distribution changes) | PSI, KS test, Wasserstein distance | PSI > 0.1 (moderate), > 0.25 (significant) | 🟢 Alert at moderate;🔴 Pause model at significant |
| **Sudden drift** | Real-time anomaly detection on feature distributions | Z-score > 3 on key features | 🔴 Immediate escalation + potential model pause |
| **Gradual drift** | Rolling30-day window comparison vs. training baseline | Consistent upward trend over 2weeks | 🟡 Schedule retraining; document in drift log |
| **Seasonal drift** | Same-period prior year comparison | Deviation from seasonal pattern | 🟢 Apply seasonal adjustment; 🟡 if novel |

**Reference Windows** (per internal drift detection frameworks):
- Training baseline: Distribution at time of model training (long-term structural drift)
- Rolling 30-day: Trailing 30 days of production data (short-term operational drift)
- Same-period prior year: Seasonal comparison (seasonality-adjusted drift)

### 5.3 Silent Model Degradation

**Symptoms**: No alert triggered, but business metrics slowly decline

| **Detection Strategy** | **Implementation** | **AI MLE Role** |
|------------------------|-------------------|-----------------|
| Scheduled offline eval against holdout set | Weekly automated evaluation pipeline | 🟢 Run eval, 🟡 flag degradation |
| Business metric correlation monitoring | Dashboard linking model metrics → business KPIs | 🟢 Monitor, 🟡 investigate disconnect |
| Prediction confidence tracking | Distribution of confidence scores over time | 🟢 Alert on confidence collapse |
| Human feedback loop integration | Track acceptance/rejection rates of model outputs | 🟢 Aggregate, 🟡 if acceptance drops |
| Canary model comparison | Shadow model running alongside production | 🟢 Compare, 🟡 recommend switch |

### 5.4 Reproducibility Issues

| **Failure Mode** | **Prevention** | **AI MLE Enforcement** |
|-----------------|---------------|----------------------|
| Non-deterministic training | Fixed random seeds, deterministic algorithms | 🟢 Auto-enforce in all training configs |
| Data version mismatch | Versioned datasets in feature store | 🟢 Refuse to train without data version lock |
| Environment drift | Containerized training environments + lockfiles | 🟢 Block training on environment mismatch |
| Missing experiment metadata | MLflow auto-logging | 🟢 Mandatory logging — fail pipeline without it |
| Undocumented preprocessing | Feature engineering pipeline versioning | 🟡 Flag unversioned transforms |

### 5.5 Feature Store Inconsistencies

| **Issue** | **Detection** | **Mitigation** |
|----------|--------------|----------------|
| Online/offline feature parity gap | Automated comparison pipeline | 🟢 Alert + detailed diff report |
| Stale features in serving | Feature freshness SLA monitoring | 🟢 Alert; 🟡 escalate if customer-facing |
| Feature duplication | Automated deduplication scan (per [DTI MLE AI1-pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~455370031/pages/6757155814)) | 🟢 Identify duplicates, 🟡 propose consolidation |
| Feature quality degradation | Statistical profiling per feature | 🟢 Auto-quarantine suspect features |

### 5.6 Deployment Rollback Scenarios

Per [CI/CD for MLOps](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6726837663) and [Agent Reliability Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AA7/pages/6097247892):

| **Trigger** | **Rollback Decision** | **Execution** |
|------------|----------------------|---------------|
| Canary quality score < threshold | 🟢 Automatic (pre-configured) | Revert to previous model version |
| Latency SLO breach post-deployment | 🟡 AI MLE recommends, human approves | Traffic shift to previous version |
| Online metric regression (A/B) | 🔴 Human decision required | Staged rollback with traffic drain |
| Data corruption detected | 🔴 Immediate human escalation | Full model and pipeline pause |
| Security vulnerability in model | 🔴 Security team + human MLE | Complete model takedown |

**Rollback Playbook:**
1. AI MLE detects anomaly → generates incident context (what changed, impact scope, affected users)
2. AI MLE proposes rollback plan with risk assessment
3. If pre-approved automated rollback: execute immediately (canary failures only)
4. If manual approval required: page human with full context + recommended action
5. Post-rollback: AI MLE runs verification, generates incident report, updates drift log

