  2 Core Responsibilities — 10 duties annotated with 🟢/🟡/🔴 autonomy tiers
    (problem formulation, feature engineering, training, eval, deployment,
    monitoring, A/B, code, incident support, knowledge production).
  3 Required Skills & Competencies — Required vs nice-to-have across
    programming, ML frameworks, domain, MLOps, plus AI-employee-specific
    competencies (spec parsing, calibrated self-eval, audit trail generation).
  4 Domain Operational Artifacts — runbooks, evaluation frameworks (AIX-Eval,
    Rovo-Eval, MRR/NDCG), query/data patterns (MLflow paths, MLFS, Statsig, ML
    Lens, Splunk), templates (model card, experiment report, decision log),
    and reference materials.
  5 Tools & Technologies — core/secondary tools matrix + dedicated Tech Stack
    & Codebase Context subsection covering ML Studio's ~18K modules, key
    architectural patterns, and ownership map.
  6 Standard Operating Procedures — three SOPs (autonomous fine-tuning loop,
    production deployment & canary, drift detection/retraining/rollback) with
    full step-by-step procedures and a performance-threshold action matrix.
  7 Collaboration & Communication — stakeholder map, comms norms
    (artifact-not-event), cadence, AI SRE peer coordination, subordinate-agent
    rules.
  8 Success Metrics & KPIs — primary metrics, AIF L3-O1-KR1 0.5/0.7/1.0 tiers,
    operational health, north-star Time-to-Delegation, agent-self KPIs.
  9 Challenges & Mitigation Strategies — technical, AI-specific,
    organizational, and operational failure modes.
 10 AI-Specific Work Philosophy — human limitations removed → raised bar,
    elevated standards table, AI-specific risks/guardrails, bounded-autonomy
    framework, 7 core tenets, anti-patterns to prevent, binding human
    oversight points.
 11 Day-One Readiness — tool access list, context packs to ingest, initial
    skill registry, six first-week demonstration tasks, and L2→L3→L4 maturity
    timeline.


Each section synthesizes (not concatenates) the three facets, resolving
overlaps on autonomy tiers, performance thresholds, and human-vs-AI
differentiation into a single consistent view. Document provenance section
traces each finding back to the originating facet.
